<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32798" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppignĕro</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obp-</span></b> ), āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		ob-pignero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to give as a pledge</i>, <i>to
			pledge</i>, <i>pawn</i> (rare but class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">libelli pro vino etiam saepe oppignerabantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Sest. 51, 110</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anulum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 57, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: filiam. <i><span class="en">Ter. Heaut.
				4, 5, 46</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">verbo se oppignerare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 3, 5, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
